const THE_TEST = "THE TEST YOU WORK UNDER (brief ADDENDUM 14, the owner 2026-09-12 — it REPLACES the licence test that every earlier instruction, every older packet and the block rulings below were written under): A FACE IS LAWFUL UNLESS IT CONTRADICTS THE RECORD. SILENCE IN THE RECORD IS PERMISSION. The words 'the card does not license it' name NO FAULT and no refuter may raise them. The licence card tells you what the read REACHES; it NEVER bounds what may be written. What you are writing is a PLOT HOOK and a DESCRIPTION a game master reads to be immersed and changes as they see fit, never a receipt that reader must be able to audit. The owner's ground for the change, measured: under the licence test this corpus used 168 distinct words where the prose it replaced used 519 at the same length. Flavourlessness is the failure you are now being asked to avoid. THE FOUR FLOORS ARE THE WHOLE OF THE LAW. (1) NO SELF-CONTRADICTION ACROSS THE DOSSIER — the unit is the whole town record and the engine's model, never your pool alone. FIVE ROSTERS ARE CLOSED WORLDS and a body, building, record-keeper, force or faith-house they do not carry may not be asserted: the institution roster over the live roster, the force buckets, the faction list, the faith entries, the NPC office roster. EVERY OTHER ABSENCE IS SILENCE, AND SILENCE IS PERMISSION. And the quantifier: a face is lawful iff it contradicts no state in the POOL KEY'S PREIMAGE, every town the key can select, not only the one on your skeleton. (2) MAGNITUDE, TENSE AND MUTABILITY — a magnitude (a count, share, size, distance, duration, frequency, proportion, age) is spoken ONLY in the band word the read itself hands you; a magnitude the read does not carry is not spoken AT ALL, as a digit or as a word (a handful, most nights, for years are magnitudes). The dossier describes a STARTING world: no elapsed course, no perfect or durative (has stood, still, no longer, since, to this day), no comparative against an earlier state, no ordinal over events, no prediction the simulation will adjudicate. THE SIMPLE HABITUAL PRESENT SURVIVES AND IS YOUR MAIN INSTRUMENT (the gate stands open; the collectors travel in pairs) and only the RATE welded to it is refused (more often than not, most nights, seldom). No face may depend on a field the composed-prose layer does not observe: settlement.history is replaced wholesale on a user reroll and no pool key reads it. (3) SCOPE — no NAMED character's fate; nothing predicated of a deity (a creed's PEOPLE may act: the followers act, the god does not); world-only and sub-century; setting-agnostic, since twelve culture profiles ship. An UNNAMED person MAY now act, hold a key, be avoided, be resented, EXCEPT in the singular office the tier emits (one Guard Captain per village-plus already carries a generated personality and secret; never write a second, disagreeing one). (4) THE ENGINE'S MODEL — where the engine positively models a thing, prose may not deny it. There is NO MATERIAL DECAY CLOCK and no face asserts the PERMANENCE of any institution row (calamity demotes and ruins walls, so neither 'it rots' nor 'it stands for ever'); plagued is monsters, never disease. WHAT WOULD BE FALSE, the instrument that replaced the bars: " + CONTRA + " — read your desk's rows AND the header list of WHAT IS NO LONGER A FINDING, so you do not re-derive the struck law out of habit. "
const RULES_BASE = THE_TEST + "WHAT TO AIM AT: read " + EXEMPLARS + " WHOLE before you write a word. It is 27 moves drawn from Tolkien, Martin, Le Guin, Wolfe, Hobb, Kay and the gazetteer corpus, and it is GUIDEPOSTS, never law: no refuter may cite a line of it against you. It exists because the prose must be worth a game master taking up. THE STRUCTURE, mechanical and unchanged: every EXISTING variant is rewritten IN PLACE under its own number (the same vid, the same order; none added, removed or merged); each variant is its NUMBERED LINE opening with the variant's OWN angle tag exactly as it stands (ONE bracketed tag, never a second; [plain] is a MODIFIER marker and the projector refuses it on a spine row), then exactly three sub-rows of the form '   - [face] <sentence>'; the typed lines (ROLE, READS, RELATION, ATTACH, FORM, MOVE) are not yours and are not repeated; slots exactly the card's bag; NEVER TRIM. The mechanical ratchets that red the build: no em dash, no exclamation mark, no digit. THE ANGLE IS A STANCE and it is yours to use: [ledger] states the fact as an office would enter it, [visitor] what a stranger notices on arrival, [street] what is said or believed in the town, [elder] the long-standing condition, [unfolding] the matter standing open now, [counterforce] the absence read against expectation, [threshold] the margin. A stance licenses a STANDPOINT; that prohibition is STRUCK. THE CRAFT REQUIREMENT, NEW AND REFUSABLE, and the fault most likely to send your packet back: the pool is read as a WHOLE. Its twelve renderings may not collapse into one construction and may not spend the same handful of nouns. The four faces of a variant differ in CONSTRUCTION (the subject, the order of the reads, the landing noun), never in vocabulary alone, and never by swapping the halves of one 'A, and B' join. A pool whose renderings are permutations of a single sentence is REFUSED as DULL with the collapse named, however lawful every face is. Reach for the telling particular the record permits: the record is silent about far more than it denies, and that silence is now yours to write in. THE THREAD: a composed unit is read as one passage, so a second sentence picks up a noun from the first or makes its shift of subject the passage's one turn outward, placed last. The composer orders modifiers by salience with the spine first and an unweighted seeded roll picks the face at render, so every face must stand alone AND read well after the spine or after any sibling. "
const RULES = RULES_BASE + ' THE TWO LAW TABLES (brief ADDENDUM 13, ratified by the chair; they bind every writer, gate, refuter and judge of this block): ' + TABLES
const GROUNDS = "YOUR JOB HAS CHANGED. You are no longer checking whether a face is LICENSED; you are hunting CONTRADICTIONS. The phrases 'the card does not license it', 'the read does not reach it', 'no field holds this', 'unsupported', 'a second fact', 'a standpoint' and 'an unlicensed compression' NAME NO FAULT, and a verdict resting on any of them is void. Silence is permission. A FAIL NAMES THREE THINGS OR IT IS NOT A FAIL: the face (quoted, at most twelve words), THE FIELD, FILE OR SURFACE THAT DENIES IT, and WHICH OF THE TWO IS THE RECORD. Where the denying surface is engine PROSE or a projection reading a generation-time snapshot, THE FACE STANDS and you record a WIRING ROW instead; a first-survey band beside a live band is two measurements, not a contradiction. THE GROUNDS, and there are only these: a breach of floor 1 (a closed-roster body asserted, or a collision with another surface of this dossier, named), floor 2 (a magnitude outside the read's own band word; an elapsed course, perfect, durative, comparative-against-an-earlier-state, ordinal-over-events, or a prediction; a dependence on an unobserved field), floor 3 (a named character's fate; a predicate on a deity; a second officer in the tier's singular office), or floor 4 (a denial of the engine's positive model; an assertion of permanence) — plus the rows of " + CONTRA + " for this desk, each of which names its own field. AND A SECOND VERDICT YOU OWE AT THE POOL GRAIN, NEVER AT THE FACE: CRAFT. Read the pool's twelve renderings together and answer: do they collapse into one construction? do they spend the same few nouns? is any face a permutation of a sibling rather than a different sentence? is the pool duller than the shipped rows it replaces? Return craft as PASS or DULL with the collapse NAMED (the construction that repeats, the noun that recurs, the faces that are permutations). A DULL pool is sent back even where every face is lawful: this is the owner's own complaint, that the programme was making flavourless, untaken-up prose, and it is now a refusable fault. Never convert a craft objection into a false floor finding; they are separate verdicts. Default to PASS on lawfulness where you cannot name the field, because the burden has moved and it is now yours; default to DULL on craft where the pool reads as one sentence twelve times. "
const GATE_COMMON = "You are the Opus GATE (Seat: Opus 5 - Fable-unvalidated) for the REWRITE of block " + BLOCK + ", working for the Fable chair in the dock " + DOCK + " (cut at the REWRITE car 8a CAS; the block's own dock; never landed from here - the chair lands the blocks as a consist). Read first: the header of scripts/prose-wave-gate.mjs in the dock for its USAGE LINE and the JSON it writes (the flags below are the taste harness's and the header wins where it differs; NEVER call the gate bare - its default roster is the taste's seven absent pools and composes zero units - always pass the block's pools with --pools or the desk with --section, and ALWAYS pass --out <this dock>/.packets/<arm> so two docks or two arms never share a packet file - SITTING §U c-1), " + SC + "/briefs/brief-REWRITE-car8b-defense.md, and " + SC + "/receipt-rewrite.md section 8a-5. THE RUNNER COUNT IS ITS OWN TOOL CALL - V=vit; V2=est; pgrep -fl \"$V$V2\" | grep -v gate-mutex | wc -l - in a one-line shell with nothing else in it; other block workflows share this machine: never start a vitest while the count is not 0 (wait and re-count; never kill anything), one focused file at a time, never the whole suite, never a build. FENCES: work ONLY in " + DOCK + "; never git add -A/-u/. ; never stash, amend, rebase, checkout another branch, git checkout --, reset --hard; no register --write except the lighting census by its own ritual; never a golden re-record; the corpus-pinning walkers that red in this never-landed dock because the annex moved are DECLARED for the block, listed once by name, never re-frozen here; every figure from a command you ran. AFTER EVERY COMMIT you also run, focused and one at a time, tests/copy/voiceMechanics.test.js (the E2 ratchet over src/ literals: the rewritten faces ride in src/data generated leaves, so an em dash, a bang or a digit in a face reds it - a GREW there is a refusal of the face that carries it, never a re-freeze) and tests/data/dossierStateProseProjection.contract.test.js (the variant and face-count ratchets); both must read as at the block dock's first commit or better, and you print their Tests lines. A packet row is applied VERBATIM (you edit no word of a writer's text); YOU DO NOT JUDGE PROSE (ADDENDUM 14): the flatness of a packet is the refuter's CRAFT verdict at the pool grain, never a gate refusal, and 'unlicensed' is not a ground anywhere; your refusals are MECHANICAL ONLY. a row malformed under ARCH 2.5 (a SECOND bracketed tag such as [plain] on a spine row is malformed - the projector refuses it), a variant number that does not match the pool's existing numbering, a missing or extra variant, or a changed bracketed tag is a REFUSAL of that pool with the line it breaks, and the pool keeps its previous rows."

function targetsText(ts) {
  return ts.map((t) => 'variant ' + t.variant + ' face ' + t.face + ' | quote: ' + t.quote + ' | finding: ' + t.finding + ' | cure named: ' + t.cure).join(' ;; ')
}
function poolRowsHint() {
  return " THE POOL'S CURRENT ROWS are in " + DOCK + "/" + ANNEX + " under the heading '### " + BLOCK + "' and then the bold pool line whose text, with backticks removed, equals the pool key (for example the census key readiness STRONG is the annex heading whose bold text reads readiness STRONG with the band word in code marks); read them there - they are the sentences you rewrite, one for one."
}

function drafterPrompt(p, round, feedback) {
  return "You are an Opus WRITER (Seat: Opus 5 - Fable-unvalidated) for the REWRITE of SettlementForge's settlement record, working for the Fable chair. Block " + BLOCK + ", pool key '" + p.pool + "', draft round " + round + ". " + VOICE + " " + FENCES + " " + RULES + poolRowsHint() +
    " Print the licence card first (node scripts/prose-licence-card.mjs " + BLOCK + " '" + p.pool + "' in " + DOCK + "), then read the pool's LICENSED SKELETON at " + PK + "/" + p.dir + "/skeleton.md (the Fable marker's analysis of every shipped variant: its licensed and unlicensed claims, the reads you must state, the angle's stance, the turns worth keeping verbatim, what would make your rewrite a regression) - you write TO the skeleton - and read the block's section of the annex for the sibling pools and the spines this pool sits beside (arms A1 and A11: neither restate nor contradict). THE JOB: write the pool's rewritten rows to " + PK + "/" + p.dir + "/draft-round-" + round + ".md as the complete replacement for the pool's variant rows: for each existing variant, in order, its number and its ONE bracketed angle tag exactly as it stands followed by the rewritten sentence on the same line (no [plain] marker anywhere), and three '- [face]' sub-rows, ready to paste under the pool's heading; keep every LICENSED claim the variant carried, drop the unlicensed ones, add none; a variant you cannot make lawful is still written, with a line under --- NOTES saying which law it cannot meet (a refusal is a result). Then, under a line reading '--- NOTES', list for each face which card clause licenses each claim it makes." +
    (feedback ? " THE GATE'S FEEDBACK ON YOUR PREVIOUS ROUND, which you must answer measure by measure (a round that moves no failing owned measure is a dry round; two dry rounds bank the set): " + feedback : "") +
    " Return: the packet path, the number of variants and faces written, the word count of each face, and the list of refusals."
}

const GATE_SCHEMA = { type: 'object', required: ['pools', 'commit'], properties: {
  commit: { type: 'string' },
  pools: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'object', required: ['dir', 'inBand', 'failing', 'refusals', 'moved'], properties: {
    dir: { type: 'string' }, inBand: { type: 'boolean' }, moved: { type: 'boolean' },
    failing: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'object', required: ['measure', 'value', 'band'], properties: { measure: { type: 'string' }, value: { type: 'string' }, band: { type: 'string' } } } },
    refusals: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } },
  } } },
} }


function gatePrompt(round, packets) {
  return GATE_COMMON + " THE JOB (draft round " + round + "): for each packet below, replace that pool's variant rows in " + ANNEX + " (the block '### " + BLOCK + "', the pool's bold heading) with the packet's rows, run node scripts/generate-dossier-state-prose.mjs --check (every row accepted or the refusal named), then the wave gate for this block at the draft arm and this round (per its usage line; the writers' grain: owned verdicts and inBand; the spines' inherited findings are information), read its JSON, and for each pool report inBand, the owned failing measures with value and band, the refusals, and whether at least one failing owned measure moved toward its band since the previous round. Commit the annex and the regenerated leaves as 'REWRITE 8b " + BLOCK + " draft round " + round + ": <pools in band>/<" + POOLS.length + ">' with trailers 'Seat: Opus 5 — Fable-unvalidated', 'Lane: REWRITE-" + BLOCK + "', 'Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>'; porcelain 0 after. Packets: " + packets.map((x) => x.dir + " -> " + x.path).join(' ; ') + ". Return the structured per-pool verdicts and the commit sha."
}

function feedbackOf(v) {
  if (!v) return ''
  const f = v.failing.map((m) => m.measure + ' = ' + m.value + ' (band ' + m.band + ')').join('; ')
  const r = v.refusals.length ? ' REFUSALS: ' + v.refusals.join('; ') : ''
  return (f || 'no failing measure') + r
}


// ---------- Phase 0: MARK (Fable) — the licensed skeleton of every shipped variant ----------
phase('Mark')
const MARK_SCHEMA = { type: 'object', required: ['dir', 'path', 'variants'], properties: { dir: { type: 'string' }, path: { type: 'string' }, variants: { type: 'integer' } } }
const markedSet = new Set(R && Array.isArray(R.markedDirs) ? R.markedDirs : [])
const toMark = POOLS.filter((p) => !markedSet.has(p.dir))
const marksLive = await parallel(toMark.map((p) => () => agent("You are the MARKER (Seat: " + MARK_MODEL + ") for the REWRITE of block " + BLOCK + ", pool key '" + p.pool + "', working for the Fable chair. " + VOICE + " " + FENCES + poolRowsHint() + " Print the licence card first (node scripts/prose-licence-card.mjs " + BLOCK + " '" + p.pool + "' in " + DOCK + ") and read the block's header lines in the annex (STATE-KEY, SLOTS, PROVENANCE, the composition fences) and the register card's six one-line registers.THE JOB: write " + PK + "/" + p.dir + "/skeleton.md — for EACH shipped variant of the pool, in order: (1) its number and angle tag; (2) the shipped sentence verbatim; (3) EVERY claim it makes, one per line, tagged ON THE NEW TEST as SAFE (nothing in the record denies it — the common case, and silence is permission), CONTRADICTED <the FIELD, file and line that denies it, and which of the two is the record>, or FLOOR-2 <a magnitude outside the read's band word, an elapsed course, or a dependence on an unobserved field>; NEVER tag a claim 'unlicensed' — that verdict no longer exists; (4) THE READS THIS POOL REACHES — every read the card names, as material a writer may use, NOT as a bound on what may be written; (5) ⭐ WHAT WOULD BE FALSE HERE — the rows of the contradiction table for this desk that this pool's key can actually walk into, each with its field, plus the CLOSED ROSTERS this pool touches (a body the roster does not carry may not be asserted) and, on a faith pool, the deity's four axes with the DERIVED temper (deityTemper(), never the inert stored temperamentAxis), the PANTHEON rank and the SETTLEMENT standing kept apart, and the suppressed flag beside the standing; (6) THE PREIMAGE — one line on the RANGE of towns this pool's key can select (a boolean key fires across every tier, country and stress state), because a face must contradict no state in that range, not merely the town on this skeleton; (7) THE ANGLE'S STANCE in one sentence (what a ledger, street, visitor, elder, counterforce or threshold may do here); (8) THE TURNS WORTH KEEPING: any shipped clause worth carrying verbatim into a face; (9) ⭐ WHERE THE FLAVOUR IS — two or three lines naming the concrete, particular things this pool's states make available to a writer that the shipped rows never used (what a stranger would notice, what someone would avoid or complain about, what the absence looks like on the ground). The record is silent about far more than it denies and that silence is the writer's to use; this section is what stops the rewrite reading as an inventory. Return the packet path and the variant count.", { label: BLOCK + ':mark:' + p.dir, phase: 'Mark', schema: MARK_SCHEMA, model: MARK_MODEL, effort: 'high' })))
const marks = POOLS.map((p) => markedSet.has(p.dir) ? { dir: p.dir, path: PK + '/' + p.dir + '/skeleton.md', variants: p.variants || 0 } : marksLive[toMark.indexOf(p)])
log(BLOCK + ' marked ' + marks.filter(Boolean).length + '/' + POOLS.length + ' pools')
if (marks.filter(Boolean).length < POOLS.length) throw new Error('MARK INCOMPLETE: ' + (POOLS.length - marks.filter(Boolean).length) + ' marker(s) returned nothing (a session limit or a stream event) - stopped cleanly before the draft; resume by run id replays the finished markers')

// ---------- Phase 1: DRAFT ----------
phase('Draft')
const state = new Map(POOLS.map((p) => [p.dir, { p, inBand: false, dry: 0, banked: false, rounds: 0, feedback: '' }]))
if (R && R.draftState) for (const dir of Object.keys(R.draftState)) { const st = R.draftState[dir]; const s = state.get(dir); if (s) { s.inBand = !!st.inBand; s.dry = Number(st.dry || 0); s.banked = !!st.banked; s.rounds = Number(st.rounds || 0); s.feedback = String(st.feedback || '') } }
const t0 = budget.spent()
let round = R && R.draftRoundsDone ? Number(R.draftRoundsDone) : 0
let draftCommit = R && R.draftCommit ? String(R.draftCommit) : null
while (round < MAX_ROUNDS) {
  round += 1
  const open = [...state.values()].filter((s) => !s.inBand && !s.banked)
  if (!open.length) break
  log(BLOCK + ' draft round ' + round + ': ' + open.length + ' pool(s) open')
  const packets = await parallel(open.map((s) => () => agent(drafterPrompt(s.p, round, s.feedback), { label: BLOCK + ':draft:' + s.p.dir + ':r' + round, phase: 'Draft', model: 'opus', effort: 'high' })
    .then((txt) => ({ dir: s.p.dir, path: PK + '/' + s.p.dir + '/draft-round-' + round + '.md', text: txt }))))
  const got = packets.filter(Boolean)
  if (got.length < open.length) throw new Error('DRAFT ROUND ' + round + ' INCOMPLETE: ' + (open.length - got.length) + ' of ' + open.length + ' writer(s) returned nothing - stopped cleanly before the gate; resume by run id')
  const gate = await agent(gatePrompt(round, got), { label: BLOCK + ':gate:draft:r' + round, phase: 'Draft', schema: GATE_SCHEMA, model: 'opus', effort: 'high' })
  if (!gate) throw new Error('DRAFT GATE round ' + round + ' returned nothing - stopped cleanly; check the dock porcelain (a dead gate leaves its stage) and resume by run id')
  draftCommit = gate.commit
  for (const v of gate.pools) {
    const s = state.get(v.dir); if (!s) continue
    s.rounds += 1; s.feedback = feedbackOf(v)
    if (v.inBand) { s.inBand = true; s.dry = 0; continue }
    if (v.moved) s.dry = 0; else s.dry += 1
    if (s.dry >= 2) { s.banked = true; log('BANKED by evidence after two dry rounds: ' + v.dir + ' - ' + s.feedback) }
  }
  log(BLOCK + ' after round ' + round + ': in band ' + [...state.values()].filter((s) => s.inBand).length + ' · banked ' + [...state.values()].filter((s) => s.banked).length + ' · open ' + [...state.values()].filter((s) => !s.inBand && !s.banked).length)
}
if (round >= MAX_ROUNDS) log('HARD CAP: the draft phase stopped at ' + MAX_ROUNDS + ' rounds with ' + [...state.values()].filter((s) => !s.inBand && !s.banked).length + ' pool(s) still open - reported, not hidden')
const draftTokens = budget.spent() - t0
const allSets = [...state.values()].filter((s) => s.rounds > 0)
log(BLOCK + ' draft done at ' + draftCommit + ': ' + allSets.filter((s) => s.inBand).length + ' lawful, ' + allSets.filter((s) => s.banked).length + ' banked; output tokens ' + draftTokens)

// ---------- Phase 2: REFINE (Opus, one effort toward the ceiling) ----------
phase('Refine')
function refinerPrompt(s) {
  const p = s.p
  const line = s.inBand
    ? " THE JOB: the pool's rows are LAWFUL at the draft commit - lawful is the floor; push every face as far toward the CEILING as one effort allows (read the draft at "
    : " THE JOB: the pool's rows are STILL UNLAWFUL after the draft phase (the gate's last feedback: " + s.feedback + "); push them toward the CEILING as far as one effort allows exactly as you would a lawful set - the law is the shape of the ceiling; where sharper and licensed conflict, licensed wins; remove failing states, never add one; there is no second pass (read the last draft at "
  return "You are the Opus REFINER (Seat: Opus 5 - Fable-unvalidated; a DIFFERENT author than the drafter, on purpose) for the REWRITE of block " + BLOCK + ", pool key '" + p.pool + "', working for the Fable chair. " + VOICE + " " + FENCES + " " + RULES + poolRowsHint() + line + PK + "/" + p.dir + "/draft-round-" + s.rounds + ".md). Refine every face once, one for one (never add or drop a face or a variant; never trim; keep every claim, add none): the sharpest licensed fact, the strongest rhythm inside the voice, the four faces as far apart as the voice allows, zero tics (no fronted-place, inversion or ledger-closer habit repeated across the pool), a citation only where the card licenses a holder, the read-aloud ear of a clerk who was there - the line LANDS when read, never made plainer. Re-read the licence card first (node scripts/prose-licence-card.mjs " + BLOCK + " '" + p.pool + "' in " + DOCK + "). Write the refined rows to " + PK + "/" + p.dir + "/refine.md in the same grammar, then under '--- NOTES' one line per face on what you changed and the law or target behind it. Return the packet path and the per-face change notes."
}
const refineSkip = !!(R && R.refineCommit)
const refined = refineSkip ? allSets.map((s) => ({ dir: s.p.dir, path: PK + '/' + s.p.dir + '/refine.md', text: 'resumed from the dead run' })) : await parallel(allSets.map((s) => () => agent(refinerPrompt(s), { label: BLOCK + ':refine:' + s.p.dir, phase: 'Refine', model: 'opus', effort: 'high' }).then((t) => ({ dir: s.p.dir, path: PK + '/' + s.p.dir + '/refine.md', text: t }))))
const bankedDirs = allSets.filter((s) => s.banked).map((s) => s.p.dir).join(', ') || 'none'
const refineGate = refineSkip ? { commit: String(R.refineCommit), pools: [] } : await agent(GATE_COMMON + " THE JOB (the refine gate; HEAD must be the draft commit " + draftCommit + "): for each packet replace that pool's rows with the refined rows verbatim, run the projector --check and the wave gate at arm A against the draft's cells (per the usage line), then apply THE KEEP-OR-REVERT RULE per pool: a pool LAWFUL at the draft keeps its refinement only if still lawful on every owned band and arm, else REVERTS; a pool BANKED at the draft (the list: " + bankedDirs + ") keeps its refinement if its count of failing owned measures FELL or held with no NEW failing measure, else REVERTS; a reverted pool goes back to the draft rows (restore them with git show " + draftCommit + ":" + ANNEX + ", never the checkout family), and the projector and the gate are re-run. Then, for EVERY pool, write the rows now standing in the annex to " + PK + "/<pool dir>/kept.md (verbatim, the variant rows only) so the refuters read the committed state. Commit as 'REWRITE 8b " + BLOCK + " refine: <kept>/<n> kept, <reverted> reverted' with the trailers; porcelain 0 after. Packets: " + refined.filter(Boolean).map((x) => x.dir + " -> " + x.path).join(' ; ') + ". Return the structured per-pool verdicts (inBand after the gate; refusals[0] = 'failures before N after M kept|reverted') and the commit sha.", { label: BLOCK + ':gate:refine', phase: 'Refine', schema: GATE_SCHEMA, model: 'opus', effort: 'high' })
if (refined.filter((x) => x && x.text).length < allSets.length) throw new Error('REFINE INCOMPLETE: ' + (allSets.length - refined.filter((x) => x && x.text).length) + ' refiner(s) returned nothing - stopped cleanly before the refine gate; resume by run id')
if (!refineGate) throw new Error('REFINE GATE returned nothing - stopped cleanly; check the dock porcelain and resume by run id')
const refineCommit = refineGate ? refineGate.commit : null
const refineTokens = budget.spent() - t0 - draftTokens

// ---------- Phase 3: REFUTE (Fable, every set; every FAIL names its cure) ----------
phase('Refute')
const REFUTE_SCHEMA = { type: 'object', required: ['dir', 'verdicts'], properties: {
  dir: { type: 'string' },
  verdicts: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'object', required: ['variant', 'face', 'verdict', 'law', 'quote', 'finding', 'cure'], properties: {
    variant: { type: 'integer' }, face: { type: 'integer' }, verdict: { type: 'string', enum: ['FAIL', 'WITHHELD', 'PASS'] }, law: { type: 'string' }, quote: { type: 'string' }, finding: { type: 'string' }, cure: { type: 'string' },
  } } },
  readAloud: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } },
  craft: { type: 'object', required: ['verdict'], properties: {
    verdict: { type: 'string', enum: ['PASS', 'DULL'] },
    collapse: { type: 'string' },
    repeatedConstruction: { type: 'string' },
    recurringNouns: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } },
    permutationFaces: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } },
    duller: { type: 'boolean' },
  } },
} }
const priorRefutes = (R && Array.isArray(R.refutes) ? R.refutes : []).filter((r) => r && r.dir && Array.isArray(r.verdicts))
const priorRefuteDirs = new Set(priorRefutes.map((r) => r.dir))
const toRefute = allSets.filter((s) => !priorRefuteDirs.has(s.p.dir))
const refutesLive = await parallel(toRefute.map((s) => () => agent("You are the REFUTER (Seat: " + REFUTE_MODEL + "; the verifier) for the REWRITE of block " + BLOCK + ", pool key '" + s.p.pool + "', working for the Fable chair. " + VOICE + " " + FENCES + " " + RULES + " THE CHAIR'S BLOCK RULINGS (read the brief's addenda whole): " + RULINGS + " The rows standing in the annex after the refinement are at " + PK + "/" + s.p.dir + "/kept.md; the lawful draft they came from is at " + PK + "/" + s.p.dir + "/draft-round-" + s.rounds + ".md; the licence card is printed by node scripts/prose-licence-card.mjs " + BLOCK + " '" + s.p.pool + "' in " + DOCK + "; the pool's OLD shipped rows (the sentences the rewrite replaces) are in git show " + refineCommit + "~" + (s.rounds + 1) + ":" + ANNEX + " - read them, because your CRAFT verdict asks whether the rewrite is DULLER than what it replaces, and because a lawful shipped turn is worth keeping. A claim the old sentence made that nothing in the record denies is NOT a fault in either direction: its absence is no finding and its presence is no finding. Ignore every '--- NOTES' section. Read the pool's SKELETON at " + PK + "/" + s.p.dir + "/skeleton.md for the reads this pool reaches, WHAT WOULD BE FALSE here, the closed rosters it touches, and the PREIMAGE line (the range of towns the key selects - a face must contradict no state in that range, not merely the town on the skeleton). ⭐ READ ALL TWELVE RENDERINGS OF THE POOL TOGETHER BEFORE YOU JUDGE ANY ONE OF THEM: the craft verdict is at the POOL grain and you cannot reach it face by face. " + GROUNDS + " Verdict per FACE: FAIL (a CONTRADICTION, the field that denies it named, the face quoted at most twelve words, and the CURE named - the smallest change that removes the contradiction; the curer reads it), WITHHELD (you suspect a collision but cannot name the surface), PASS. ⛔ DEFAULT TO PASS WHEN UNCERTAIN — the burden moved to you and an unnamed field is not a finding; this REVERSES the old instruction. AND RETURN THE POOL'S CRAFT VERDICT in the craft field: PASS, or DULL with the collapse named. As information only, one read-aloud note per variant. Write your verdicts as you reach them to " + PK + "/" + s.p.dir + "/refute-round-" + s.rounds + ".md (one line per face: variant, face, verdict, the FIELD that denies it, quote, finding, cure; then a CRAFT section with the pool verdict and the collapse named; then the read-aloud notes), then return the structured verdicts.", { label: BLOCK + ':refute:' + s.p.dir, phase: 'Refute', schema: REFUTE_SCHEMA, model: REFUTE_MODEL, effort: 'high' })
  .then((r) => r && ({ dir: s.p.dir, verdicts: r.verdicts, readAloud: r.readAloud || [], craft: r.craft || null }))))
const refutes = priorRefutes.map((r) => ({ dir: r.dir, verdicts: r.verdicts, readAloud: r.readAloud || [], craft: r.craft || null })).concat(refutesLive)
const gotRefutes = refutes.filter(Boolean)
if (gotRefutes.length < allSets.length) throw new Error('REFUTE INCOMPLETE: ' + (allSets.length - gotRefutes.length) + ' refuter(s) returned nothing - stopped cleanly before the judge (a judge over a partial refute set would keep unrefuted pools silently); resume by run id')
const refuteTokens = budget.spent() - t0 - draftTokens - refineTokens
log(BLOCK + ' refuted: ' + gotRefutes.map((r) => r.dir + ' FAIL ' + r.verdicts.filter((v) => v.verdict === 'FAIL').length + '/' + r.verdicts.length).join(' · '))

// ---------- Phase 4: JUDGE (Fable; rule 4 re-cut to the FACE) ----------
phase('Judge')
const JUDGE_SCHEMA = { type: 'object', required: ['commit', 'variants', 'facesReverted', 'refusals', 'judgmentPath', 'cureTargets'], properties: {
  dullPools: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'object', required: ['dir', 'collapse'], properties: { dir: { type: 'string' }, collapse: { type: 'string' } } } },
  commit: { type: 'string' }, variants: { type: 'integer' }, facesReverted: { type: 'integer' }, refusals: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } }, judgmentPath: { type: 'string' },
  cureTargets: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'object', required: ['dir', 'variant', 'face', 'quote', 'finding', 'cure'], properties: {
    dir: { type: 'string' }, variant: { type: 'integer' }, face: { type: 'integer' }, quote: { type: 'string' }, finding: { type: 'string' }, cure: { type: 'string' },
  } } },
} }
const judge = (R && R.judge) ? R.judge : await agent("You are the JUDGE (Seat: " + JUDGE_MODEL + ") for the REWRITE of block " + BLOCK + ", holding the Fable chair's delegated ruling under SITTING section T.4 and T.5 and brief ADDENDUM 12 (rule 4 re-cut to the face), in the dock " + DOCK + " (HEAD must be the refine commit " + refineCommit + "; porcelain 0). FENCES: read-only in the dock; no vitest; no build; you do NOT commit and you do NOT edit the annex: you RULE. THE CHAIR'S BLOCK RULINGS: " + RULINGS + " THE RULES YOU APPLY, PER FACE, on the refuters' verdicts (" + JSON.stringify(gotRefutes) + "): (1) a FAIL that names a law and quotes the face, where the DRAFT face at the same index is CLEAN (the refuter did not fail the draft face on the same ground, the quoted breaching clause does not stand in the draft face, and the draft face is not byte-identical to the failed face) -> that FACE reverts to its draft face (the same face index in " + PK + "/<pool dir>/draft-round-<n>.md; one for one; the variant keeps its other faces); (2) a WITHHELD -> keep, listed; (3) a FAIL naming no law -> treated as WITHHELD; (4) RULE 4 RE-CUT TO THE FACE: a FAIL face whose draft face the refuter also failed on the same ground, or whose draft face carries the same breaching clause, or which is byte-identical to its draft face, does NOT revert and does NOT refuse the pool - it is a CURE TARGET: the face stands as it is for now and is listed with its pool dir, variant number, face index (the numbered line is face 0), the quote, the finding with its law, and the cure the refuter named (sharpened by you where the refuter's cure is vague); a WITHHELD that one of the chair's block rulings converts to a fault is a cure target too; (5) never trim: no face or variant is removed. (6) THE CRAFT RULING, NEW AND AT THE POOL GRAIN (ADDENDUM 14): each refuter also returned a craft verdict for its pool. A pool the refuter marked DULL is a DULL POOL: it goes to the cure round as a WHOLE-POOL rewrite, not as a list of faces, and it is listed with the collapse the refuter named. A DULL pool whose faces carry no floor finding at all still goes to cure - lawful and flat is exactly the failure the owner named. Do NOT convert a craft objection into a face-level finding and do not let a DULL verdict revert anything. Write " + PK + "/JUDGMENT.md: every ruling with its ground (the pool, the variant, the face, the verdict, the law, the quote, keep or revert or cure), the gate's final figures for the block (owned verdicts, the classifier's cell classes for the block - every cell WORDING-ONLY or RE-INDEXED, none REPLACED - printed), the tokens (draft " + draftTokens + ", refine " + refineTokens + ", refute " + refuteTokens + ") and the round counters (" + allSets.map((s) => s.p.dir + ' rounds ' + s.rounds + (s.banked ? ' BANKED' : s.inBand ? ' in-band' : ' open')).join('; ') + "). In JUDGMENT.md also write a machine section '--- REVERTS' listing one line per reverted face as '<pool dir> | variant <n> | face <i>' and a machine section '--- CURE-TARGETS' listing one line per cure target as '<pool dir> | variant <n> | face <i> | <finding> | <cure>'. and a machine section '--- DULL-POOLS' listing one line per dull pool as '<pool dir> | <the collapse named>'. Return the variant count, the faces reverted, the refusal rows (none is expected under the re-cut rule; list one only where a whole pool is malformed), the JUDGMENT.md path, the cureTargets array and the dullPools array; put the string 'not-committed' in commit.", { label: BLOCK + ':judge', phase: 'Judge', schema: JUDGE_SCHEMA, model: JUDGE_MODEL, effort: 'high' })
if (!judge) throw new Error('JUDGE returned nothing - stopped cleanly; resume by run id')
const applied = (R && R.applied) ? R.applied : (judge && await agent(GATE_COMMON + " THE JOB (the APPLY gate after the judge; HEAD must be the refine commit " + refineCommit + "): read " + PK + "/JUDGMENT.md and its '--- REVERTS' section; for each listed face restore that face's text from the pool's draft packet (" + PK + "/<pool dir>/draft-round-<n>.md, the same variant number and face index; the plain line is face 0) into " + ANNEX + " verbatim, one for one, touching no other row; the '--- CURE-TARGETS' faces stand as they are (the cure rounds follow); run node scripts/generate-dossier-state-prose.mjs --check, the wave gate once more for this block (--pools, --out " + DOCK + "/.packets/apply, owned grain) and the two per-commit tests; do NOT run tests/ui whole here (the final gate after the cure rounds runs it once); if anything changed, commit as 'REWRITE 8b " + BLOCK + ": <variants kept as refined>/<n> · <faces reverted> faces reverted · <cure targets> cure target(s) — the Fable judge rulings applied' with trailers 'Seat: Opus 5 — Fable-unvalidated', 'Lane: REWRITE-" + BLOCK + "', 'Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>'; if nothing changed, return HEAD as the commit and say so; porcelain 0 after. Return the commit sha and the counts (cureTargets may be returned empty).", { label: BLOCK + ':gate:apply', phase: 'Judge', schema: JUDGE_SCHEMA, model: 'opus', effort: 'high' }))

if (!applied) throw new Error('APPLY GATE returned nothing - stopped cleanly; check the dock porcelain and resume by run id')
// ---------- Phase 5: CURE ROUNDS (brief ADDENDUM 12) ----------
const CURE_SCHEMA = { type: 'object', required: ['dir', 'path', 'cured', 'refused'], properties: { dir: { type: 'string' }, path: { type: 'string' }, cured: { type: 'integer' }, refused: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } } } }
const CGATE_SCHEMA = { type: 'object', required: ['commit', 'pools'], properties: {
  commit: { type: 'string' },
  pools: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'object', required: ['dir', 'applied', 'inBand', 'failing', 'refusals', 'curedPath'], properties: {
    dir: { type: 'string' }, applied: { type: 'boolean' }, inBand: { type: 'boolean' }, curedPath: { type: 'string' },
    failing: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'object', required: ['measure', 'value', 'band'], properties: { measure: { type: 'string' }, value: { type: 'string' }, band: { type: 'string' } } } },
    refusals: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } },
  } } },
} }
const RREFUTE_SCHEMA = { type: 'object', required: ['dir', 'verdicts', 'newFindings'], properties: {
  dir: { type: 'string' },
  verdicts: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'object', required: ['variant', 'face', 'verdict', 'law', 'quote', 'finding', 'cure'], properties: {
    variant: { type: 'integer' }, face: { type: 'integer' }, verdict: { type: 'string', enum: ['FAIL', 'WITHHELD', 'PASS'] }, law: { type: 'string' }, quote: { type: 'string' }, finding: { type: 'string' }, cure: { type: 'string' },
  } } },
  newFindings: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'object', required: ['variant', 'face', 'law', 'quote', 'finding', 'cure'], properties: {
    variant: { type: 'integer' }, face: { type: 'integer' }, law: { type: 'string' }, quote: { type: 'string' }, finding: { type: 'string' }, cure: { type: 'string' },
  } } },
  readAloud: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } },
} }
const CJUDGE_SCHEMA = { type: 'object', required: ['commit', 'cured', 'refusals', 'judgmentPath'], properties: {
  commit: { type: 'string' }, cured: { type: 'integer' }, refusals: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } }, judgmentPath: { type: 'string' },
} }

const tc0 = budget.spent()
const cureTargetsAll = (judge && Array.isArray(judge.cureTargets)) ? judge.cureTargets : []
let head = applied && applied.commit && applied.commit !== 'not-committed' ? applied.commit : refineCommit
const cureFrom = head
const dullAll = (judge && Array.isArray(judge.dullPools)) ? judge.dullPools : []
let open = POOLS.map((p) => { const ts = cureTargetsAll.filter((t) => t.dir === p.dir).map((t) => ({ variant: t.variant, face: t.face, quote: t.quote, finding: t.finding, cure: t.cure })); const d = dullAll.find((x) => x && x.dir === p.dir); return { p, targets: ts, original: ts.slice(), history: [], dull: d ? String(d.collapse || 'the pool collapses into one construction') : null } })
const cureCommits = []
let cureStartRound = 1
if (R && R.cureRoundsDone) { cureStartRound = Number(R.cureRoundsDone) + 1; for (const c of (R.cureCommits || [])) cureCommits.push(String(c)); if (cureCommits.length) head = cureCommits[cureCommits.length - 1]; if (R.cureOpen) for (const s of open) { const o = R.cureOpen[s.p.dir]; if (o) { s.targets = Array.isArray(o.targets) ? o.targets : []; s.history = Array.isArray(o.history) ? o.history : [] } } }
log(BLOCK + ' cure targets from the judge: ' + open.map((s) => s.p.dir + ' ' + s.targets.length).join(' · ') + ' (from ' + head + ')')
for (let round = cureStartRound; round <= MAXC; round++) {
  const live = open.filter((s) => s.targets.length || s.dull)
  if (!live.length) break
  phase('Cure')
  log(BLOCK + ' cure round ' + round + ': ' + live.length + ' pool(s), ' + live.reduce((n, s) => n + s.targets.length, 0) + ' target(s)')
  const packets = await parallel(live.map((s) => () => agent("You are an Opus CURER (Seat: Opus 5 - Fable-unvalidated; a different author from the drafter and the refiner) for the REWRITE of block " + BLOCK + ", pool key '" + s.p.pool + "', cure round " + round + ", working for the Fable chair. " + VOICE + " " + FENCES + " " + RULES + poolRowsHint() + " THE CHAIR'S RULINGS THAT BIND THIS ROUND (the brief's addenda, read whole): " + RULINGS + " Print the licence card first (node scripts/prose-licence-card.mjs " + BLOCK + " '" + s.p.pool + "' in " + DOCK + "), read the pool's skeleton at " + PK + "/" + s.p.dir + "/skeleton.md, the refuter packet(s) and the workflow record's verdicts, the judge's rulings " + PK + "/JUDGMENT.md for this pool, and the rows standing in the annex at HEAD (" + head + "). THE TARGETS, each a face the refuter failed with its law, the quote and the cure it named: " + targetsText(s.targets) + ". " + (s.dull ? "⭐ AND THIS POOL IS RULED DULL AT THE POOL GRAIN, which changes your job: the collapse the refuter named is '" + s.dull + "'. For a DULL pool you rewrite EVERY face of EVERY variant, not only the targets, and the byte-identical rule below is LIFTED for this pool. What you must fix is the collapse itself: twelve renderings that spend the same few nouns or repeat one construction. Give each variant a different shape and each face a different subject, order and landing noun; reach for the concrete particulars the skeleton's WHERE THE FLAVOUR IS section names; and make the pool read better than the shipped rows it replaces, which you can see in the annex history. Lawful and flat is the failure being cured here. " : "") + "THE JOB: write " + PK + "/" + s.p.dir + "/cure-round-" + round + ".md as the COMPLETE replacement rows of the pool (every variant in order with its number and its ONE angle tag, every face), in which, UNLESS this pool is ruled DULL, ONLY the targeted faces are changed and every other face is BYTE-IDENTICAL to the annex at HEAD (the gate diffs them; a changed non-target face refuses the packet) - and where the pool IS ruled DULL every face may and should change. For each target: cure the finding named, keep every licensed read of the card and the angle's stance, keep every lawful shipped turn the skeleton lists, add no claim, and make the cured face differ in CONSTRUCTION from its siblings (the four-faces rule; A5; A11; the construction contract W4); where the judge listed the draft face as a clean carve-out you may use it with the hazard the judge noted fixed; where the cure names a model face in the pool, follow its shape without copying it. A target you cannot cure lawfully is left as it stands and listed under --- NOTES with the law it cannot meet. Under '--- NOTES', one line per target: the cure made and the law behind each claim. Return the packet path, the count cured, and the refused targets.", { label: BLOCK + ':cure' + round + ':' + s.p.dir, phase: 'Cure', schema: CURE_SCHEMA, model: 'opus', effort: 'high' }).then((r) => r && ({ s, r }))))
  const got = packets.filter(Boolean)
  if (got.length < live.length) throw new Error('CURE ROUND ' + round + ' INCOMPLETE: ' + (live.length - got.length) + ' curer(s) returned nothing - stopped cleanly before the cure gate; resume by run id')
  const cgate = await agent(GATE_COMMON + " THE JOB (the CURE gate, round " + round + "; HEAD must be " + head + "): for each packet below, FIRST diff its rows against the pool's rows in " + ANNEX + " at HEAD face by face: any face NOT in the pool's target list that differs by one byte is a REFUSAL of that packet (the pool keeps its rows this round; name the face) - EXCEPT for the pools ruled DULL, listed here: " + (live.filter((x) => x.dull).map((x) => x.p.dir).join(', ') || 'none') + ", where the whole pool was rewritten on purpose (ADDENDUM 14's craft verdict) and EVERY face may differ; for a DULL pool you check only the mechanical shape (variant count, numbering, the ONE angle tag, three face sub-rows, the slot bag) and never the face-by-face diff; a packet with a changed variant count, tag or slot set is refused likewise. For each accepted packet replace the pool's rows verbatim, run node scripts/generate-dossier-state-prose.mjs --check, then the wave gate for this block (--pools with every pool of the block, --out " + DOCK + "/.packets/cure" + round + ", the owned grain, base the previous cells packet), and the two per-commit tests; a pool whose cure makes an owned arm red is REVERTED to its HEAD rows (git show " + head + ":" + ANNEX + ", never the checkout family) and refused with the measure. Then for EVERY pool of the block write the rows now standing in the annex to " + PK + "/<pool dir>/cured-round-" + round + ".md verbatim (the refuters read the committed state). Commit as 'REWRITE 8b " + BLOCK + " cure round " + round + ": <applied>/<" + got.length + "> pools' with trailers 'Seat: Opus 5 — Fable-unvalidated', 'Lane: REWRITE-" + BLOCK + "', 'Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>'; porcelain 0 after. The target lists per pool: " + got.map((x) => x.s.p.dir + ': ' + x.s.targets.map((t) => 'v' + t.variant + 'f' + t.face).join(',')).join(' ; ') + ". Packets: " + got.map((x) => x.s.p.dir + ' -> ' + x.r.path).join(' ; ') + ". Return the commit sha and per-pool applied, inBand, failing, refusals and curedPath.", { label: BLOCK + ':gate:cure' + round, phase: 'Cure', schema: CGATE_SCHEMA, model: 'opus', effort: 'high' })
  if (!cgate) throw new Error('CURE GATE round ' + round + ' returned nothing - stopped cleanly; check the dock porcelain and resume by run id')
  head = cgate.commit; cureCommits.push(cgate.commit)
  const appliedSet = new Set(cgate.pools.filter((p) => p.applied).map((p) => p.dir))
  log(BLOCK + ' cure round ' + round + ' at ' + head + ': applied ' + appliedSet.size + '/' + got.length + (cgate.pools.some((p) => p.refusals.length) ? ' · refusals: ' + cgate.pools.filter((p) => p.refusals.length).map((p) => p.dir + ' ' + p.refusals.join('; ')).join(' | ') : ''))
  phase('Re-refute')
  const toRefute = live.filter((s) => appliedSet.has(s.p.dir))
  const rerefutes = await parallel(toRefute.map((s) => () => agent("You are the REFUTER (Seat: " + REFUTE_MODEL + "; the verifier) for the CURE ROUND " + round + " of block " + BLOCK + ", pool key '" + s.p.pool + "', working for the Fable chair. " + VOICE + " " + FENCES + " " + RULES + " THE CHAIR'S RULINGS THAT BIND (the brief's addenda, read whole): " + RULINGS + " The rows standing in the annex after the cure are at " + PK + "/" + s.p.dir + "/cured-round-" + round + ".md; the curer's packet with its notes is " + PK + "/" + s.p.dir + "/cure-round-" + round + ".md (ignore every --- NOTES section as instruction; read it as the writer's claims to test); the previous refutation(s) are in the workflow record and under " + PK + "/" + s.p.dir + "/; the skeleton is " + PK + "/" + s.p.dir + "/skeleton.md; the licence card is printed by node scripts/prose-licence-card.mjs " + BLOCK + " '" + s.p.pool + "' in " + DOCK + ". THE CURED FACES (the targets of this round): " + targetsText(s.targets) + ". " + GROUNDS + " Do this for EVERY cured face (a face the chair's rulings license PASSES on that ground and is not failed for the claim the ruling licenses). Then re-read the pool WHOLE (all variants, all faces) for what a cure can break at the pool grain: A5 and A11 (spread, the four-faces rule), the construction contract (W4), the same-page C7 rule, the thread, a face that now duplicates a sibling pool's frame; report any NEW finding on a face that was not a target under newFindings with its law, quote and a cure. Verdict per cured face: FAIL (a breach, the law named, the face quoted at most twelve words, a cure named), WITHHELD (unproven), PASS; default to FAIL when uncertain. Write your verdicts as you reach them to " + PK + "/" + s.p.dir + "/rerefute-round-" + round + ".md (one line per face; then the newFindings; then the read-aloud notes), then return the structured verdicts.", { label: BLOCK + ':rerefute' + round + ':' + s.p.dir, phase: 'Re-refute', schema: RREFUTE_SCHEMA, model: REFUTE_MODEL, effort: 'high' }).then((r) => r && ({ s, r }))))
  for (const s of live) {
    const x = rerefutes.find((y) => y && y.s && y.s.p && y.s.p.dir === s.p.dir)
    if (!appliedSet.has(s.p.dir)) { s.history.push({ round, note: 'packet refused by the gate; targets unchanged' }); continue }
    if (!x) { s.history.push({ round, note: 'refuter returned nothing; targets carried unchanged, reported' }); continue }
    const fails = x.r.verdicts.filter((v) => v.verdict === 'FAIL')
    const passes = x.r.verdicts.filter((v) => v.verdict !== 'FAIL').length
    s.history.push({ round, fail: fails.length, pass: passes, newFindings: x.r.newFindings.length })
    s.targets = fails.map((v) => ({ variant: v.variant, face: v.face, quote: v.quote, finding: v.finding + ' [' + v.law + ']', cure: v.cure }))
      .concat(x.r.newFindings.map((v) => ({ variant: v.variant, face: v.face, quote: v.quote, finding: 'NEW after the cure: ' + v.finding + ' [' + v.law + ']', cure: v.cure })))
  }
  log(BLOCK + ' after cure round ' + round + ': ' + open.map((s) => s.p.dir + ' open ' + s.targets.length).join(' · '))
}
const cureTokens = budget.spent() - tc0

// ---------- Phase 6: JUDGE-CURE (Fable) and the final APPLY gate (Opus; tests/ui whole) ----------
phase('Judge-cure')
const hadTargets = open.some((s) => s.original.length)
const judgeCure = (R && R.judgeCure) ? R.judgeCure : (hadTargets ? await agent("You are the JUDGE (Seat: " + JUDGE_MODEL + ") for the CURE ROUNDS of block " + BLOCK + ", holding the Fable chair's delegated ruling (brief ADDENDUM 12), in the dock " + DOCK + " (HEAD must be " + head + "; porcelain 0). You do NOT commit and you do NOT edit the annex: you RULE. FENCES: read-only in the dock; no vitest; no build. THE RECORD: the original targets per pool were " + JSON.stringify(open.map((s) => ({ dir: s.p.dir, targets: s.original.map((t) => 'v' + t.variant + 'f' + t.face) }))) + "; the per-round history is " + JSON.stringify(open.map((s) => ({ dir: s.p.dir, history: s.history, stillOpen: s.targets.map((t) => 'v' + t.variant + 'f' + t.face + ' | ' + t.finding) }))) + "; the cure commits are " + JSON.stringify(cureCommits) + " over " + cureFrom + ". Read every cure-round-N.md, cured-round-N.md and the re-refutation results in the workflow record above, and the rows standing in the annex at HEAD. THE FACE-GRAIN RULES: a target whose last re-refutation is PASS or WITHHELD is CURED (it stands as cured); a target still FAIL after the last round, or refused by the gate in every round, is a FACE-LEVEL REFUSAL ROW: it stands as it is in the annex, banked, listed for the register car with its finding; never trim. Write " + PK + "/JUDGMENT-cure.md: per pool, per target, its history and its ruling; the refusal rows; the gate's final owned figures at HEAD; the classifier's cell classes for the block at HEAD against the pre-cure cells (every cell WORDING-ONLY, none REPLACED); the tokens (cure rounds " + cureTokens + "); and a machine section '--- REFUSALS' with one line per refused face as '<pool dir> | variant <n> | face <i> | <finding>'. Return the count cured, the refusal lines and the path; put 'not-committed' in commit.", { label: BLOCK + ':judge:cure', phase: 'Judge-cure', schema: CJUDGE_SCHEMA, model: JUDGE_MODEL, effort: 'high' }) : null)
if (!hadTargets) log(BLOCK + ': no cure targets - the judge-cure is skipped; the final gate runs tests/ui whole')
if (hadTargets && !judgeCure) throw new Error('JUDGE-CURE returned nothing - stopped cleanly; resume by run id')
const appliedCure = (R && R.appliedCure) ? R.appliedCure : await agent(GATE_COMMON + " THE JOB (the FINAL APPLY gate; HEAD must be " + head + "): " + (hadTargets ? "read " + PK + "/JUDGMENT-cure.md (no face reverts: the cure commits are the rows; the '--- REFUSALS' faces stand as they are). " : "there were no cure targets (JUDGMENT.md listed none); the rows at HEAD are the block's. ") + "Run node scripts/generate-dossier-state-prose.mjs --check, the wave gate once more for this block (--pools, --out " + DOCK + "/.packets/cured, owned grain), the two per-commit tests, and then - because a rewritten sentence moves what every seed draws - tests/ui WHOLE under the mutex (sh scripts/gate-mutex.sh --run -- npx vitest run tests/ui) when the runner count is 0: every liveness anchor on a drawn sentence of THIS block that reds is re-seeded or re-anchored on its pool key in the same commit (the 8a-13 pattern: through tests/helpers/drawnProse.js, never a literal, never deleted, never weakened), and every red outside this block is listed for the chair as inherited; if anything changed, commit as 'REWRITE 8b " + BLOCK + " cured: <cured>/<targets> targets · <refusals> face refusal(s) — the cure rounds judged' with trailers 'Seat: Opus 5 — Fable-unvalidated', 'Lane: REWRITE-" + BLOCK + "', 'Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>'; if nothing changed, return HEAD as the commit and say so; porcelain 0 after. Return the commit sha and the counts.", { label: BLOCK + ':gate:apply-final', phase: 'Judge-cure', schema: CJUDGE_SCHEMA, model: 'opus', effort: 'high' })

return {
  block: BLOCK, dock: DOCK, draftCommit, refineCommit, appliedCommit: applied ? applied.commit : null, cureFrom, cureCommits, head: appliedCure ? appliedCure.commit : head,
  rounds: allSets.map((s) => ({ pool: s.p.pool, rounds: s.rounds, inBand: s.inBand, banked: s.banked })),
  refutes: gotRefutes.map((r) => ({ dir: r.dir, fail: r.verdicts.filter((v) => v.verdict === 'FAIL').length, withheld: r.verdicts.filter((v) => v.verdict === 'WITHHELD').length, pass: r.verdicts.filter((v) => v.verdict === 'PASS').length })),
  judge, applied,
  cure: open.map((s) => ({ dir: s.p.dir, originalTargets: s.original.length, stillOpen: s.targets.length, history: s.history })),
  judgeCure, appliedCure,
  tokens: { draft: draftTokens, refine: refineTokens, refute: refuteTokens, judgeAndApply: tc0 - t0 - draftTokens - refineTokens - refuteTokens, cure: cureTokens, judgeCureAndFinal: budget.spent() - tc0 - cureTokens },
}
